# ZSP500 instruction encodings, recovered from the disassembler in the
# vendor's ZSP debugger DLL (abizsp.dll, from the RK27xx SDK) and checked
# on the RK27xx with hwstub. Documented in the ZSP500 DSP programming
# manual: https://www.rockbox.org/wiki/pub/Main/Rockchip27xx/ZSP500_DSP_Programming_Manual.pdf
#
# pattern: bit15..0 of first halfword [then bit15..0 of second]; 0/1 fixed, x ignored, letters = fields (MSB first)
# syntax placeholders: {a} unsigned, {a:s} signed, {2a}/{4a} pair/quad register number, {a+6} a6/a7,
#   {a:TABLE[+k]} name from table (index = field + k), {n+1} count, {o:rel8|rel16} branch target
# lines are tried in order; 16-bit forms come first
0000 cccc oooo oooo                       | {c:br_cond} {o:rel8}
0110 010a aaa1 1nnn                       | cexer (r{a},nz,u) { } !{n+1}
0110 010a aaa1 0nnn                       | cexer (r{a},nz,nu) { } !{n+1}
0110 010a aaa0 1nnn                       | cexer (r{a},z,u) { } !{n+1}
0110 010a aaa0 0nnn                       | cexer (r{a},z,nu) { } !{n+1}
0110 0110 cccc 1nnn                       | cexe ({c:cexe_cond},u) { } !{n+1}
0110 0110 cccc 0nnn                       | cexe ({c:cexe_cond},nu) { } !{n+1}
0110 0111 cccc 1nnn                       | cexes ({c:cexe_cond},u) { } !{n+1}
0110 0111 cccc 0nnn                       | cexes ({c:cexe_cond},nu) { } !{n+1}
0000 0000 0000 0000                       | nop
